# Migration from Firebase to MySQL

We need to completely remove Firebase from the frontend and connect the application to the provided Node.js + Express backend, using a MySQL database as the single source of truth.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> This is a major architectural overhaul that touches both the frontend and backend. We are going to permanently remove Firebase and replace it with a self-hosted custom backend.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The MySQL database needs to be running locally on port 3306 with credentials `root`/`root` and database name `projectflow_edu` as per your instructions.

## Open Questions

1. Are you currently running a MySQL server on your machine? If not, please start it so the backend can connect.
2. The schema file uses `bcrypt` hashes (`hashed_pass_here`). During migration, I'll update the backend to generate real bcrypt hashes for new signups. For the seeded dummy users (like `hod@college.edu`), should I update their passwords to a known plain text password (e.g., `password123`) so you can log in as them?

## Proposed Changes

### Database Setup
- Execute `database/projectflow_edu_schema.sql` into the local MySQL database.
- Update the seeded users with a bcrypt hash of `password123` so we can log in with them.

---

### Backend (Node.js/Express)

#### [MODIFY] backend/.env
Add the provided DB credentials and JWT_SECRET.

#### [NEW] backend/src/controllers/authController.js
Implement JWT-based authentication (register, login, getMe) using `mysql2` pool.

#### [NEW] backend/src/controllers/projectController.js
Implement CRUD for projects referencing the `projects` table.

#### [NEW] backend/src/controllers/taskController.js
Implement CRUD for tasks referencing the `tasks` table.

#### [NEW] backend/src/controllers/documentController.js
Implement file metadata management. Use dummy local file paths for uploads.

#### [MODIFY] backend/src/app.js
Register new routes for tasks and documents. Add file upload middleware placeholder.

---

### Frontend (React)

#### [DELETE] frontend/src/lib/firebase.js
Completely remove Firebase initialization.

#### [NEW] frontend/src/lib/api.js
Create an Axios instance with an interceptor that automatically attaches the JWT token from `localStorage` to requests.

#### [MODIFY] frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx
Replace Firebase logic with API calls to `POST /api/auth/login`, `POST /api/auth/register`, and `GET /api/auth/me`. Store JWT token in `localStorage`.

#### [MODIFY] frontend/src/pages/auth/Login.jsx & Signup.jsx
Adapt to the new AuthContext API (removing Firebase specific error handling).

#### [MODIFY] frontend/src/pages/student/StudentProjects.jsx & ProjectDetails.jsx
Fetch and mutate projects via `api.get('/projects')` and `api.post('/projects')` instead of Firestore.

#### [MODIFY] frontend/src/pages/student/StudentKanban.jsx
Fetch and mutate tasks via `api.get('/tasks/project/:projectId')` instead of Firestore.

#### [MODIFY] frontend/src/pages/student/StudentDocumentation.jsx
Fetch and mutate documents via `api.get('/documents/project/:projectId')` instead of Firebase Storage.

#### [MODIFY] frontend/.env & package.json
Remove `VITE_FIREBASE_*` variables and `firebase` dependency. Add `VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api`.

